+## Customer and issuing-key binding — 2026-10-26
+
+The validated customer access token is forwarded server-to-server for quote,
+checkout and recovery. Refresh remains in Route Handlers and persists the rotated
+encrypted auth cookie before checkout. The signed checkout cookie now contains an
+opaque binding to customer, tenant and issuing API key. Switching customer or key
+cannot read, verify, cancel, replay or replace that browser's checkout.
+
+Older checkout cookies without the binding fail closed with403. Do not silently
+clear an outstanding attempt or start another charge to bypass this boundary;
+reconcile it with the store. Another account using the same browser also needs
+its own clean checkout context after the original obligation is resolved.
+Automatic recovery under an old API key is not implemented: keep the issuing key
+available until its accepted attempts are drained/reconciled, then rotate and
+require sign-in. Restoring the original approved connection/account can recover
+its bound cookie; do not share keys with the browser.
+
+Local evidence comes from actual Wyn route/client/session/schema modules calling
+the actual DrinksHarbour Express/Mongo API on a disposable29128 fixture. Only Next
+request-cookie context and provider transport are replaced. This proves local
+contracts, not hosted Next cookie transport or a hosted Paystack roundtrip.
