+
+The actual checkout Route Handler validated the customer but omitted its access
+token on the REST checkout call, creating guest/unlinked backend orders. It also
+allowed a second signed-in customer in the same browser to inspect the first
+customer's signed checkout handle. Both failures were reproduced through actual
+route modules against an isolated synthetic DrinksHarbour HTTP/Mongo fixture.
+
+Corrected six focused server modules: drinks REST client, checkout-customer,
+checkout-session and quote/create/status Route Handlers. Only post-validation
+(and post-refresh) access tokens are forwarded server-to-server; the signed
+checkout cookie binds customer, tenant and issuing key. Browser responses expose
+no tokens. New unit coverage checks owner binding. Legacy unbound checkout cookies
+and customer/key changes reject403 rather than silently create another charge.
+Drain/reconcile old attempts before key replacement; transparent old-key recovery
+is not implemented. See docs/checkout.md for this migration limit.
